WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
FUYUKI BRIDGE, JAPAN
10 YEARS AGO

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:42.060
ARCHISORTE MANSION, ENGLAND
7 YEARS AGO

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.970
Wh-Who are you people?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.060
Why did you suddenly abduct me?

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.560
I'm a secret fan of yours,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.820
Waver Velvet.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.200
And who the hell are you?

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:57.700
I am Reines El-Melloi Archisorte.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.290
I'm the sister-by-succession
of Kayneth El-Melloi Archibald,

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:06.250
your former teacher and participant
in the Fourth Holy Grail War.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.710
Now you understand who I am, right?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.760
In terms of actual blood relationships,
I'm his niece.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.470
Then, you brought me here for...

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.890
Oh no.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.300
I'm not interested in revenge or anything.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.600
I just want to ask you about something
I've been wondering about for some time.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.020
You participated in the Holy Grail War,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.780
the Magecraft ritual that took place in Fuyuki,

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.280
the battle to win the omnipotent wish granter,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.570
did you not?

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.070
I did.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.450
My elder brother lost
and died a cruel death.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.080
Yes.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.120
And then I lost.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.960
My life was spared by luck, and here I am!

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.710
Whether it was luck or not aside,

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.930
six months later, you went back
to London, borrowed tons of money

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.220
to purchase the El-Melloi Class
my brother left behind.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:06.730
Do you want to call me a thief
who stole his mentor's inheritance?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.190
Not in the least!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.440
You're a very popular teacher!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.360
I just want to know something.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.950
What made you do it?

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.450
I have a right to know that,

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.490
don't I?

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.450
It's kind of a long story.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:34.340
Did you know that a human being
can't last long when hung upside down?

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.970
The exact figure is disputed,
but most agree that after three hours,

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.220
the heart can't endure
the strain of blood flow reversal

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.600
and simply stops.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.230
Okay!

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:53.230
THE RUINS OF BABYLON, IRAQ
SEVERAL MONTHS AFTER THE FOURTH HOLY GRAIL WAR

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.200
This is...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.070
Babylon.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.160
This is the city that was built
by one of the first kings, Gilgamesh,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.460
and also the city where Iskandar,
the conqueror of the world, passed away.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.950
Dammit!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.450
Dammit! Move!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.200
I have to get to the doctor!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.370
What's wrong?

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.250
This piece of junk
won't start up! Dammit!

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.130
I was told the make was Japanese.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:03.590
Let me take a look.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.840
H-Hey!

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.140
It's cool.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.930
This is his city.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.850
If there's trouble, I can't overlook it.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.520
As I suspected.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.570
The spark plug's dead.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.070
You just need this
to get to the doctor, right?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.400
Yeah!

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:22.990
Okay.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.530
<i>In that case...</i>

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.080
No way!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.540
Is this good enough?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.040
Y-Yeah!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.050
Listen, whatever you do,
don't turn off the engine.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.670
It's a temporary fix.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.260
Might as well ask the doctor
to get that spark plug replaced.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.430
Thanks, foreign bro!

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.230
Hey, you're a Mage, huh?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.480
That's right.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.400
Thought so.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:03.360
These are suspension-type Mystic Eyes!

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.820
I was at the Clock Tower, too.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.780
I may not look it, but in this area,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.330
I'm well known as Barzan,
the returnee from London, you know?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.040
I don't know you.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.410
I'm just looking for an inn.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.960
If you want a class reunion,
go somewhere else.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.960
It's a combination of Mystic Eyes
with conditioned Magecraft.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.220
Kind of impressive, huh, buddy?

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.970
I doubt it.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.220
If you need to crash somewhere,
stay at my place. You cool with that?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.720
Yeah?

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.650
All right, this is your room!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.230
It's no three-stars,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.070
but try to make yourself at home.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.030
Hey!

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.330
A Mage's body is the ideal resource.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:55.370
I plan to make full use of it,
so don't damage the merchandise.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.250
Treating me like a sacrifice?

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.420
See you later, buddy.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.170
I'll have someone bring your meal later.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.710
Go to Hell!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.380
Dammit!

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.590
I bet you bombed at the Clock Tower,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.050
so now, you're just putting on airs
here in the sticks!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:16.770
Dammit!

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.270
Calm down, Waver!

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.600
The Mystic Eyes effect
has long worn off!

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.730
And I'm sure this is just a basic barrier!

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.650
Hey, could you keep it down?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.240
Screw you!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.070
I-It's you...

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.370
Waver?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.200
Why, it's Waver Velvet!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.460
Melvin...

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.290
That's right!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.960
Your old friend from school, Melvin Weins!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.130
Oh boy, I'm glad I could see you!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.180
Don't puke all of a sudden!

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.980
So, you're still in the habit
of vomiting blood at any given moment.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.770
Actually, what are you even doing here?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.690
That old boy sold me on making
a "riskless and profitable investment,"

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.820
so I came to Iraq but ended up here.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.030
It was him, huh?

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.530
That Barzan guy.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.580
I had visions of beautiful Arabic women

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.040
but got ripped off to the tune
of 30 million dollars, too.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.710
You really are scum, you know?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.670
Whoa, that's no way
to talk to a friend, Waver.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.380
I don't remember us
ever becoming friends!

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.550
Oh.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.680
Well, what about you?

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.300
Didn't you go to Japan

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.060
with the money you borrowed from me?

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.520
Yeah.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.060
Hey, Melvin!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.020
THE CLOCK TOWER, LONDON
10 YEARS AGO

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.610
That last time, you said
you'd give me money or anything

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.400
if it got you an amusing story, remember?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.740
Of course!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.910
In order to get to hear
an interesting story,

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.910
I'm ready to pay anyone
with money from my mom's purse!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.330
Then, lend me money for a trip to Japan!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.330
Japan?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.250
I'll turn the whole Clock Tower on its head!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:08.420
So, I'm dying to hear your interesting story.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.170
How was Japan?

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.470
Resting your head on a geisha's lap
must've been something, huh?

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.260
I'm sorry. I don't have
that kind of story to tell.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.770
I was useless

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.140
in that Holy Grail War!

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:28.070
So, the story you were going to tell me
was about the Holy Grail War?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.280
Yes.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.240
You heard about it, too?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.570
Just a rumor...

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.160
that Professor Kayneth
died a horrible death.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.410
Then, you didn't know
my brother had died.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.920
Since the Holy Grail War ended
without a winner,

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.960
I assumed he was dead.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.710
Well, I'm sure there was no way
for you to verify it.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:56.220
At any rate, his fiancée, Sola-Ui,
who was accompanying him, also died.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.600
Apparently, his body
was in a ghastly condition.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.810
It seems hardly any of his
Magical Crests could be recovered.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.520
What a waste.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.900
Who killed Kayneth?

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.910
I heard it was a Saber-class Heroic Spirit.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:21.410
Is it true that they summoned
former heroes as familiars?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.160
That's what the Holy Grail War is.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.460
Legendary Heroic Spirits killing each other.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.840
Let's get out of here.

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.260
Waver?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.760
There's no point in hanging out.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.640
I can't believe you wore out
the joints of the door using Magecraft!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.600
I'm not that naïve and foolish
to try to destroy the door itself.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.730
By disregarding fixed ideas,

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.820
you find all manner of opportunities.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.360
Have you somewhat changed?

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.240
Maybe you lost your virginity.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:01.450
I haven't lost—

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.410
I'm interested in that, too.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.210
So, have you lost it?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.000
Who cares about that?

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.250
Then,

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.380
we found a workshop
deep down the passage.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.850
What's going on?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.640
He's tricked these people

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.020
into digging up the ruins of Babylon.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.310
He says it might be the crypt of Iskandar.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.780
Well, it's lucky for us
that they're busy excavating.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.110
Let's get out of here.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.320
What did you just say?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.740
I said let's get out of here.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.700
No! About this place!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.710
I said he thinks
Iskandar might be buried here.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.040
I'm gonna level this place!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.340
Wait, you're the one who said
there's no sense in hanging out!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.670
And now I said I'm gonna destroy it!

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.970
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
{Rail Zeppelin} Grace note

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:04.100
Wow! I wish I had a front row seat to that!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.770
Are you a hero
from a Hollywood movie or what?

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.640
I wasn't even close to a hero.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.480
Are you really gonna do this?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.900
If you don't like it, escape yourself!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.650
Yeah, as if!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.990
You know very well how sickly I am!

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.740
Yeah, I remember.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.740
Besides, I can't waste the chance to see

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.000
such a spectacle in the VIP seat!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.210
Then, help me!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:33.920
What?

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.050
That's all I have to do?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:48.640
Damn! Not again!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.640
Can't use this one anymore!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.480
You'll be a sacrifice!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.520
Hold it there!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.320
What you're doing
violates the Clock Tower's rule

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.400
to conceal the Mystics of Magecraft.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.320
I can't ignore it!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.570
How shocking! Are you stupid or what?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:10.160
Even though you managed to escape,
you came back to be a captive.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.540
The captive of my Mystic Eyes!

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.880
Well, this is actually convenient.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.460
Your Magical Circuits are third-rate,

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.590
but good enough to be
pilot lights of the workshop.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.180
Don't worry, I won't waste any.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.260
Too bad I'm third-rate!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.720
But so are you, right, buddy?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.980
These Mystic Eyes are invincible.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.480
With the power of Mystic Eyes
and the Relic of Iskandar I'm about to obtain,

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.820
I'll surpass even the Clock Tower!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:45.240
Is it a "The Clock Tower which didn't
recognize my genius" kind of thing?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.410
What?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:50.120
Yeah, I've seen all these spells before.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.540
But everything is different
between London and Babylon. Leylines, too.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.960
You're hopeless here.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:56.960
Bastard!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.460
What do you know about my Magecraft?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:00.670
I know.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.470
I know the true meaning
of fellow Mages killing each other!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.300
All right!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.100
I'm going to teach you thoroughly
about that terror and agony!

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.920
What did you do?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:46.590
All I did was destroy the balance
of Leyline and activate evil spirits.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:53.100
All of your spells are no more
than cheap copies of the Lords'.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.890
Demolish one blind spot
and this is what happens.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.650
B-But I still have my Mystic Eyes!

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.230
In a battle of Magecraft...

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.320
Idiot!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:12.160
It's not like it's necessary
for one Mage to defeat another!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.410
What?

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.020
What's wrong, Waver?

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:41.940
I'm sorry.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.730
The money...

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.400
This is all I can repay you.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:52.160
I can't deliver on that promise
of an amusing story, either.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.870
I really was stupid and powerless.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:58.710
But...

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.460
But there's something
I want to do no matter what.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:03.710
So...

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.010
So?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.880
Lend me money!

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:14.220
I want to buy the El-Melloi Class
that lost its teacher!

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.220
Why?

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.270
I've been thinking about it
all this time. And...

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.230
I'm responsible for his death!

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.190
I don't have collateral or a guarantee!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.480
But please!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.820
Sure!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.990
You don't have collateral!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.620
You don't have a guarantee!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.790
But there's one reason
I would loan you the money!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:39.870
Name it.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.130
We're friends.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.960
We'll become best friends, Waver!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.960
What are you talking about?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.720
Isn't that wildly out of context?

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.630
There's nothing wild about it!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.760
Your words moved me!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.140
Sure!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.890
And if we're best friends, I'll wait
as long as you need to repay me!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:06.980
No! Don't puke in my clothes!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.030
And there you have it.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:10.990
I see.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:24.250
And then, you've sustained
the El-Melloi Class for the last three years.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:25.960
No. I should say you've succeeded.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.170
Stop that sarcasm.

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.300
I somehow managed
to keep it barely alive.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:36.640
Still, whatever the truth is,
you've preserved the El-Melloi Class

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:40.350
in that den of evil, the Clock Tower,
for the past three years.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.060
It wouldn't be an understatement
to call it a miracle.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:48.980
But now, I return to my original question.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.240
Tell me, Waver Velvet.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.410
You're going to all this trouble
to manage the class, but...

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.490
why on earth do you do that?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.250
Because your brother-by-succession,
Lord El-Melloi...

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:06.040
my mentor, died...

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.800
due to my reckless and foolish behavior.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.630
We didn't have an amicable relationship,

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.390
and it's not that he held me
in high esteem!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:22.060
But the fact is I learned a lot in his class.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.150
If so, I can't take away
the opportunity to learn

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.440
from students who are like I used to be.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.700
Please forgive me!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.830
I just didn't think
your reason would be so serious!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:48.880
But yes, true. If you hadn't stolen
the valuable Relic of Iskandar,

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:52.630
my elder brother
may have lived a little longer.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.760
Exactly.

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.760
I wasn't able to make full use of this.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.260
I couldn't become the Master
of that King of Conquerors.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.640
I acknowledge my sin.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.770
I ask only that you spare my life!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.610
What's this?
Aren't you supposed to say,

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:14.690
"If you're not satisfied, you can kill me"?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:18.280
It's because there's something
I need to do in the name of that king.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:22.790
Understood.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.660
Then, since we're here,

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:29.420
I think I'll exploit your sense of guilt
with several demands!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:35.130
Right now, the El-Melloi faction
is suffering from crushing debt.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.930
The amount is equivalent
to the budget of a Hollywood blockbuster.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.680
You're telling me to take over that debt?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:46.060
Yes. If you're going to take responsibility,
it has to start with that debt.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.020
All right.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.150
Seriously?

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.780
Would I accept a sum like that as a joke?

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.030
Th-Then, the second demand!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.610
What is it?

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.660
You heard, didn't you?

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.660
About my elder brother's Magical Crest...

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.660
or the El-Melloi Family's
original Magical Crest...

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.540
Only approximately
ten percent could be recovered.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.130
Yes. The essence of a Mage.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.050
And it was destroyed.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.760
Even if our family Tuner works
on restoring it, it will take three generations.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:22.300
At this rate,
the family will be finished.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.220
Got it. I'll do something about that, too.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.810
Wh-What?

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.480
Are you sure?

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.400
Aren't you making promises
without due consideration?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:37.360
Maybe bugs got implanted in your brain
during that Holy Grail War!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.200
Not at all!

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:41.740
I told you I would take responsibility!

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:42.990
I see.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.740
All right, I'll move on
to the most important thing.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.700
You know about the Lords, right?

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.460
Mages of the highest rank
who rule the Mage's Association.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.380
There's no way I don't know that.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.460
Yes.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:02.050
To the El-Melloi faction,
the position of Lord is absolute.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.100
Because if you lose
the entitlement to expel a Lord,

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.270
you won't be considered part
of the Clock Tower's inner circle.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:12.310
As a compromise resolution,
I've been chosen as the new head,

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.810
but I'm obviously too young, right?

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:18.650
So, would you keep my seat warm

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:22.030
as the Lord of El-Melloi
until I reach a suitable age?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.320
I don't mind doing it,

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.620
but what exactly do you want me to do?

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.040
Until I grow up and reach adulthood,

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:33.620
I will have someone
do the work of a Lord in my stead.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:34.880
Wait!

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.540
So, you mean...

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.340
That's right.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.090
I'm sure that diplomacy
with the other Lords will be super boring,

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.430
but I'm counting on you...

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.470
the new Lord El-Melloi.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.220
Or...

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.480
shall I call you...

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:54.810
my dear...

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.360
Elder Brother?

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.030
I'm to become...

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.820
Kayneth's successor?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.580
I have one condition.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.580
What is it?

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:13.580
I want you to add "II" to "Lord El-Melloi."

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.790
Otherwise, the name
is a heavy burden for me to bear.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.880
One that is only suitable for my mentor.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.920
I thought you hated my elder brother.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.760
Personally, I'm not fond of him, even now.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:27.890
But...

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.760
I respect him as a Mage.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.350
Most of all,

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.060
there is someone I should pursue!

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:55.330
<i>That's right.</i>

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.420
<i>Even though the Holy Grail War is over,</i>

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.460
<i>as absurd as it is, life goes on.</i>

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>As far as it goes on,</i>

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:09.390
<i>I have to struggle to survive.</i>

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
<i>Until the day I reach...</i>

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:41.250
<i>the farthest ocean you wanted to see!</i>

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:48.260
THE CLOCK TOWER, LONDON
THE PRESENT

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:51.550
Sir!

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:53.430
You're back!

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:54.470
Yes.

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:57.350
The fallout from the Izelma business
is finally over.

00:22:57.600 --> 00:22:59.270
That's good to hear.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:02.230
You've got a visitor.

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:04.650
Them?

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:09.780
Welcome home, buddy!

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.450
You have troublesome affairs
for me again, don't you?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.250
Of course, my dear Elder Brother.

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:19.960
I want you to help me with something
as payment for the debt.

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.960
I'll make sure all this
won't be a waste for you!

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:24.750
Tell me about it.

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:26.960
What kind of case is this?

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:28.670
Of course,

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:31.970
this is a difficult case

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:34.640
fit for Lord El-Melloi II.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
EPISODE 1:
Babylon, the Condemned,
and the Memories of the King
